    <string-array name="odmr_tutorial_titles">
        <item>Set up base plate</item>
        <item>Insert laser module</item>
        <item>Position mirror</item>
        <item>Insert beam splitter</item>
        <item>Insert lens</item>
        <item>Position NV sample</item>
        <item>Align photodiode</item>
        <item>Coarse alignment</item>
        <item>Fine alignment</item>
        <item>Microwave antenna</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="odmr_tutorial_texts">
        <item>Place the UC2 base plate on a stable, vibration-free surface. All optical components will be mounted on it.</item>
        <item>Insert the laser module (532 nm green diode) into the designated cube. Do NOT turn it on yet! Have safety glasses ready.</item>
        <item>Place the 45° mirror so it deflects the laser beam by 90° toward the sample.</item>
        <item>Insert the beam splitter with longpass filter. It separates the excitation light (green) from the fluorescence light (red).</item>
        <item>Place the converging lens in the beam path. It focuses the laser onto the NV diamond sample.</item>
        <item>Place the NV diamond on the XY stage. Roughly position it in the focal point of the lens.</item>
        <item>Place the photodiode (TSL2591) behind the beam splitter. It receives the red fluorescence light.</item>
        <item>Turn on the laser. Start monitoring above. Slowly move the sample until a signal appears. Target: status \"Good\".</item>
        <item>Optimise sample and lens position for maximum intensity while watching the intensity history. Target: status \"Optimal\".</item>
        <item>Position the microwave antenna close to the sample. Switch to the Sweep tab and run a first ODMR scan.</item>
    </string-array>

